 43%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $28K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Satellogic Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $535M market cap on $18M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +43% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -273% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $34M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +14.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 24% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 7.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +14.6% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 184% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 308% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Satellogic (NASDAQ:SATL) Stock Jumps 9% \u2013 Time to Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/27/satellogic-nasdaqsatl-stock-jumps-9-time-to-buy.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793120847.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Counterpoint Mutual Funds LLC Purchases 135,401 Shares of Satellogic Inc. $SATL","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/18/counterpoint-mutual-funds-llc-purchases-135401-shares-of-satellogic-inc-satl.html","date":"2026-10-18","timestamp":1792311067.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Satellogic President Frank Dixon Whitworth III Awarded 356,193 RSUs in October 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/satellogic-president-frank-dixon-whitworth-iii-a